{"body":"This is the actual line behind the first issue above. `hasOfferedColour` comes back false in two different situations: when there's no colour option at all, and when there is one but every value got filtered out. Only the second case is the problem, since it also turns off the suppression and lets the old picker show through.","line":null,"path":"overrides/app/pages/product-detail/index.tsx"}
{"body":"Same thing as the general comment. This used to switch between circle and square depending on which attribute it was, and now it's just always square. This looks like it changed without realizing `product-view` is shared across cart, wishlist, and bonus product too, since none of those pass the new suppress flag, so they're all getting square swatches now as a side effect. Worth checking where else a component is used before changing something this central to it. This should go back to picking circle or square based on the attribute like before, so it only affects this PDP.","line":null,"path":"overrides/app/components/product-view/index.tsx"}
{"body":"Quick one: the comment says this doesn't exist as a public export elsewhere, but it actually does, it's exported from `product-utils.js`, and this PR already imports two other things from that same file (`getPriceData` and `getUpdateBundleChildArray`). Might be simpler to just use the existing one instead of keeping a second copy around, especially since they don't behave quite the same (the original one handles a missing `imageGroups` fine, this one throws), which is an easy thing to lose track of later.","line":null,"path":"overrides/app/utils/filterImageGroups.ts"}
{"body":"The disabled chevron here just fades out with `opacity: 0.3`. I checked the same element on the other version of this feature against Figma directly, and the spec actually wants a colour change, not a fade. This goes against how disabled states are handled everywhere else in this design system, which is always through colour tokens, not opacity, so this needs to switch to the colour based approach to stay consistent.","line":null,"path":"overrides/app/components/product-view/colourSwatches/colourSwatches.css.ts"}

